# =============================================================================
# list<T, size 1…∞> — a kernel needs a finite size
# =============================================================================
# This exemplum intentionally fails to compile.
#
# What this teaches:
#   • A kernel unrolls every slot of a list up to its maximum and masks the dead ones, so the maximum must be a finite constant.
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Leaving the upper end open in a kernel signature; write `size 1…8`.

